"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[3290],{23290:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"08-rabota-deneg","title":"Lesson 08. Inflation and rules: Money should work, but not immediately","sourceFingerprint":"d087b1e553a6760e9d6d855fabfcc28c74fbf7558ad3402e8b5cdc7c30ba1833","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## Inflation and rules"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"Money should work, but not immediately"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"Suppose debt is controlled, a cushion is building and part of every salary goes to a separate account. What should happen to that money next? The answer has 2 seemingly contradictory parts. Leaving it idle lets inflation consume it. Yet rushing it into the market is premature."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"### What inflation does to savings"},{"id":"b005","markdown":"According to Rosstat, Russian annual inflation in September 2026 was 6.35%. On average, what cost 100 RUB a year earlier now costs around 106 RUB. That seems small, like a phone battery losing a couple of percent of capacity annually: barely noticeable now, but after several years it no longer lasts until evening."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"Suppose you put 300 000 RUB aside for a new work laptop and leave it in a drawer. If inflation remains at 6.35%, its value in today’s prices becomes:"},{"id":"b007","markdown":"| After | Purchasing power |\\n| 3 years | around 249 000 RUB |\\n| 5 years | around 221 000 RUB |\\n| 10 years | around 162 000 RUB |\\nThe same banknotes remain, but after 10 years they buy a laptop roughly half as capable as the one originally planned."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"Official inflation uses an average national basket. Your basket differs, so personal inflation can too. Check Rosstat for individual goods’ price histories; explore inflation’s effect on savings in this lesson’s simulator."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"DRAWER MONEY LOSES PURCHASING POWER. NOW 300 000 RUB. 3 YEARS 249 000 RUB. 5 YEARS 221 000 RUB. 10 YEARS 162 000 RUB. INFLATION 6.35% ANNUALLY, IN TODAY’S PRICES. What will idle money be worth?"},{"id":"b010","markdown":"Amount saved: 300 000 RUB. Annual inflation: 6.35%. After:"},{"id":"b011","markdown":"3 years, 5 years, 10 years: 162 086 RUB."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"In today’s prices."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"The same notes remain, but they buy 46% less. Starting inflation is the latest annual figure in the Bank of Russia data, September 2026."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"### Compound interest"},{"id":"b015","markdown":"The same mechanism can work for you. When interest accrues on both invested money and earlier interest, growth accelerates. This is compound interest. Example: save 7 000 RUB monthly, around 7% of average take-home pay, at 12% annually, with interest added every month."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"| After | Own contributions | Account value |\\n| 3 years | 252 000 RUB | around 305 000 RUB |\\n| 10 years | 840 000 RUB | around 1 630 000 RUB |\\nAfter 10 years almost half is interest rather than contributions. Compare starting dates over a 15-year horizon: one person saves 7 000 RUB monthly now, another starts in 5 years, and both finish together."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"- Start now: contributions of 1 260 000 RUB, account value around 3.5 million RUB."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"- Start in 5 years: contributions of 840 000 RUB, account value around 1.6 million RUB."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"The contribution difference is 420 000 RUB, but the outcome differs by almost 1.9 million RUB. A 5-year delay costs more than half of the final amount."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"Important: this is simplified. It assumes 12% throughout, which will not persist. Analysts surveyed by the Bank of Russia expect an average key rate around 12.8% in 2027 and lower later. Deposit rates follow it, though the central bank also forecasts lower inflation."},{"id":"b021","markdown":"Saving monthly for 15 years: what does an early start achieve?"},{"id":"b022","markdown":"Monthly saving 7 000 RUB. Annual rate 12.0%. The second person starts 5 years later. Start now: contribute 1 260 000 RUB, finish with 3 532 032 RUB. Start after 5 years: contribute 840 000 RUB, finish with 1 626 374 RUB. Contributions differ by 420 000 RUB, outcomes by 1 905 658 RUB. Delay costs 54% of the final amount. Simplified calculation: the rate will not persist throughout, and interest is added monthly."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"### Nominal and real returns"},{"id":"b024","markdown":"A deposit paying 13% with inflation at 6.35% does not make you 13% richer: inflation takes its share first. Real return is the ratio of the deposit growth factor to the price growth factor, minus one. A 13% deposit rate with 6.35% inflation yields approximately 6.3% a year. This is a good result, but it does not always happen. In 2021–2022, deposit rates sometimes fell below inflation, and savers lost purchasing power even while receiving interest."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"When someone boasts about returns, immediately ask what inflation was."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"Figures at the time of writing"},{"id":"b027","markdown":"Average maximum deposit rate at the 10 largest banks, second ten-day period of October: 13.06%. Annual inflation in September 2026: 6.35%. Deposit return above inflation, approximately rate minus inflation: +6.7%. Text figures are dated to writing. Check current values on the official Bank of Russia website."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"### A checklist before the first investment"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"Before a long journey a sensible driver checks oil, tyres and brakes, not because the car is untrustworthy but because breaking down 300 km from town costs far more than half an hour at the garage. A first investment is similar, except reversing the decision may be impossible."},{"id":"b030","markdown":"Check these 5 items before buying a first stock. 1. I understand the product. This is the most frequently broken rule."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"I have designed interfaces for years, including finance, and know the process from inside. You open a bank app to renew a deposit and see a bright “higher return than deposits” banner beside the button. Behind it may be investment-linked or endowment life insurance, a structured product or “capital-protected fund”. Designers call these dark patterns: a large bright button promotes the bank’s preferred choice, while small grey text contains the conditions."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"These products are not deposits and do not have DIA insurance. Fees are often high and hidden in terms, while early exit can cost part of principal. You would not sign a rental agreement unread. Apply the same rule to finance: if you cannot explain to a friend within 2 minutes how the product earns and when you could lose money, do not buy."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"2. I do not believe in risk-free returns. An insured-bank ruble deposit currently carries the lowest risk, yielding near the key rate, around 13%. Anything promising significantly more has greater risk, without exception. A “trader”, crypto project or “private investors’ club” promising stable monthly percentages is almost certainly a pyramid. The Bank of Russia website lists businesses showing signs of illegal activity; checking takes a minute."},{"id":"b034","markdown":"3. The money is mine, not the bank’s. Borrowing at 25% to buy stocks that “will definitely rise” guarantees paying 25% for an uncertain outcome. Market and crypto leverage is even more dangerous. The exchange lesson in MakeCash Academy’s Crypto Basics course explains typical outcomes."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"4. I will not need this money for around 5 years. Renovation money needed next year belongs in a deposit, not the market. Markets can do anything in a year; over 5–10 years the chances of a reasonable outcome are substantially better."},{"id":"b036","markdown":"5. The foundation is ready. No expensive debt remains, because repaying a 25% loan saves a guaranteed 25% annually, unlike any stock; lessons 4 and 5. The cushion is complete, because stocks can fall 30–40% in a year and the first setback without reserves forces a sale at the worst moment; lesson 6."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"If even one item is unchecked, postpone the journey."},{"id":"b038","markdown":"### Where money belongs right now"},{"id":"b039","markdown":"While taking this module, saved money has 3 destinations: early repayment of expensive debt, daily-balance savings accounts and deposits at insured banks. Investing begins in the next module, once the foundation is ready."},{"id":"b040","markdown":"### The essentials"},{"id":"b041","markdown":"- At 6.35% inflation, 300 000 RUB in a drawer becomes roughly 162 000 RUB of today’s purchasing power after 10 years."},{"id":"b042","markdown":"- Compound interest works in the opposite direction. Time is crucial: a 5-year delay can cost over half the final amount."},{"id":"b043","markdown":"- Look at real return: rate minus inflation."},{"id":"b044","markdown":"- Before investing, check understanding, rejection of risk-free promises, own money, a horizon from 5 years, repaid debts and a complete cushion."},{"id":"b045","markdown":"Next lesson examines making the bank pay you more than you pay it."}],"terms":[{"id":"asv","term":"Deposit Insurance Agency (DIA)","definition":"The state mechanism paying a depositor up to 1.4 million RUB per bank if its licence is revoked or it fails. Holding more than this in one bank is therefore imprudent."},{"id":"dosrochnoe-pogashenie","term":"Early repayment","definition":"The best way to reduce loan overpayment. At a 21% rate, an early payment provides a guaranteed 21% “return” unavailable from investments."},{"id":"inflyatsiya","term":"Inflation","definition":"A rise in the general price level. In practice: there is more money and the same quantity of goods, so each item costs more. You have not become richer; price tags have simply risen."},{"id":"klyuchevaya-stavka","term":"Key interest rate","definition":"The rate at which the central bank lends to banks. The main monetary-policy tool and the economy’s “price of money”. A higher rate makes loans more expensive and slows inflation."},{"id":"realnaya-dokhodnost","term":"Real return","definition":"Return adjusted for inflation. An 18% deposit with 9% inflation means a real 9%. A 5% deposit with 9% inflation means minus 4%."},{"id":"slozhnyy-protsent","term":"Compound interest","definition":"Interest earning interest. The long-term investor’s main ally: 10 000 RUB invested now for 20 years is worth more than 100 000 RUB invested in 10 years."},{"id":"strakhovanie-vkladov","term":"Deposit insurance","definition":"A state guarantee to repay depositors up to a certain amount if a bank fails. In Russia, 1.4 million RUB per bank through the Deposit Insurance Agency."},{"id":"dokhodnost","term":"Yield","definition":"The annual percentage an investment actually earns at today’s price. A bond’s price and yield move in opposite directions: falling price means rising yield. Government-bond yields influence loan and deposit rates."},{"id":"kreditnoe-plecho","term":"Leverage","definition":"Borrowing makes a position larger than your own money: with 10x leverage, $1 000 opens a $10 000 position. Price changes affect your money 10 times as strongly, in both directions."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"08-rabota-deneg-q1","q":"A deposit pays 13% annually and inflation is 6.35%. What is the approximate real return?","options":["Around 6.3%","13%","19.35%"],"correct":0},{"id":"08-rabota-deneg-q2","q":"Someone offers “guaranteed” 5% monthly. What is most likely?","options":["An ordinary bank deposit","A sign of a pyramid or very high hidden risk","Government bonds"],"correct":1},{"id":"08-rabota-deneg-q3","q":"A bright banner beside “Renew deposit” offers investment-linked life insurance with higher returns. Which statement is true?","options":["It is the same deposit under another name","These products always beat deposits","It is not a deposit, has no DIA cover, and fees and exit terms must be examined before purchase"],"correct":2}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);